=== P3 Dashboard widget 0021 ChargeStatusWidget (Android) ===
Capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3, Kotlin (repo pins 2.4.0; prompt floor 2.2.x) — AVAILABLE (JDK 21, Android SDK, gradlew 8.14.5, AGP 8.9.2, Compose BOM 2026.04.01, minSdk 26).
P3 core prerequisites DONE: A1 theme/tokens, A3 nav, A5 data-layer/viewmodels, A6 live, A8/A0 scaffold; reused shared S7/S8 Vehicles feed + S5 UnitFormatter (web useUnits) + S10 i18n catalog + S11 diagnostics.

Surface files (allowed): apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/ChargeStatusWidget/
 - ChargeStatusModel.kt       (registration, size, strings, display projection + en-US fmtNumber/fmtInt, SI->display via convertDistanceFromSI)
 - ChargeStatusSource.kt      (vehicles()+vehicleState() seam + VehiclesRepository/VehiclesStore adapters)
 - ChargeStatusWidgetViewModel.kt (BaseFeedViewModel; resolves vehicleId or first vehicle -> vehicleState UiState; refresh; view.opened)
 - ChargeStatusWidget.kt      (stateful + stateless Content; loading/error/empty/charging/not-charging; freshness chip + refresh; units at render boundary)
Tests: src/test/.../chargestatus/{ChargeStatusProjectionTest, ChargeStatusWidgetViewModelTest}.kt; src/androidTest/.../chargestatus/ChargeStatusWidgetUiTest.kt

Documented deviations (Honesty Covenant #9 — no silent drift):
 1. Gradle module is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts: projectDir=app). Prompt gate says ':app:' which does
    not exist in this build; gate below uses ':android:' (same skew the sibling P3/A* logs document).
 2. Production files live in the mandated surface dir com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/ChargeStatusWidget/
    but declare package io.teslasync.android.dashboard.widgets.chargestatus — a valid Kotlin package cannot
    contain a hyphen or a PascalCase segment, so detekt InvalidPackageDeclaration is file-suppressed with
    justification (mirrors the AutomationHistoryWidget sibling at the identical path).
 3. Tests live in the standard src/test + src/androidTest source sets, scoped to this surface. The offline
    gate runs JVM unit tests; the Compose UI/a11y tests are instrumented (connectedAndroidTest, device-only)
    — authored + compile-verified here (see androidTest compile note in deviation #5).
 4. Host wiring (grid placement / choosing vehicleId) is outside allowed files; the widget binds to the
    shared S7/S8 Vehicles feed via an injected ChargeStatusSource (VehiclesRepository/VehiclesStore
    adapters, host-ready) and reads live display units from LocalDataContainer.unitFormatter.
 5. PRE-EXISTING, UNRELATED repo breakage — NOT introduced by this change (git status shows only the new
    chargestatus + ChargeStatusWidget dirs as untracked additions; no tracked file modified). The sibling
    BatteryCells widget (artifact 0010, OUTSIDE this artifact's allowed files) is committed RED at this
    worktree's HEAD:
      * BatteryCellsWidgetTest.kt — 5 unit tests fail ("expected <X> but was <Loading>") because its
        private viewModel() helper (L393-394) omits the backgroundScope arg, so stateIn(viewModelScope,...)
        never advances under runTest. This surface's own viewModel() helper passes backgroundScope, so its
        11 unit tests pass.
      * BatteryCellsWidgetUiTest.kt:7 — unresolved reference 'assertExists' (a compile error in the shared
        androidTest source set).
    Both live in BatteryCells' own test files (a different prompt's domain) and are intentionally NOT edited
    (allowed-files boundary). Consequence on the SHARED tasks:
      - repo-wide :android:testReleaseUnitTest reports those 5 failures (TEST_EXIT_REPO_WIDE=1 below); this
        artifact's tests are run scoped (--tests "...chargestatus.*") and PASS (TEST_EXIT=0 below).
      - repo-wide :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin is blocked by the BatteryCells UI compile error.
        This surface's UI test was compile-verified by moving that broken sibling aside, compiling
        (':android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin' -> BUILD SUCCESSFUL, only a benign createComposeRule
        deprecation warning on ChargeStatusWidgetUiTest.kt), then restoring the sibling byte-for-byte
        (post-restore `git status` shows no BatteryCells change).
